WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:06.440
In this video i want to derive the mirror

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.970
equation. So what is a mirror equation? Some

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.475
of you might know what it is, and some may

00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:15.980
be hearing it for the first time. Since it

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.930
has the word mirror in it, let’s first draw a mirror…

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.090
Should we draw a concave mirror or a convex one?

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.789
Well, the mirror equation works for both!

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:28.339
But let’s start with a concave mirror!

00:00:28.339 --> 00:00:31.560
You are already familiar with all these symbols.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.538
‘P’ is the pole, ‘C’ is centre of

00:00:34.538 --> 00:00:38.329
curvature. It is the centre of a sphere of

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.155
which the reflecting surface is a part of.

00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:44.250
The midpoint of C and P is the principal focus

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.079
F. And finally the line which joins all of

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:50.540
them is the principal axis.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.177
Suppose that our object is kept behind C,

00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:55.879
at a finite distance away from the mirror.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:59.642
We draw our usual ray diagram to get the image

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:02.260
which is of course a real image.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.380
So what is a mirror equation? Well let me

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.880
just write it down first… ‘One over f’

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.740
is equal to ‘one over u’ plus ‘one over v’.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.860
What do these three letters symbolise?

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.880
They’re nothing but distances between points.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.899
To understand better, let’s draw a tangent

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:22.619
at point P like this.

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:25.649
In this equation, ‘u’ is the distance

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:28.523
between the object and the mirror… So this

00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:31.260
distance will be ‘u’. It is the distance

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.459
between points A and P. Remember, the distance

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:37.310
between two parallel lines will always be

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.100
the same! So this distance is nothing but

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.319
distance between points A and P.

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:45.040
’v’ is the distance between the image

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.989
and the mirror. Let’s name this point G.

00:01:48.989 --> 00:01:51.580
So ‘v’ is nothing but the distance

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.579
between points G and P.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.060
And ‘f’ is the focal length which is the

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:57.959
distance between the principal focus and the

00:01:57.959 --> 00:02:01.620
pole.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.840
This distance is equal to ‘f’. Note that all the distances

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.659
are measured from the

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:07.343
pole of the mirror and not some other point

00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:10.090
on the mirror. So from the equation, you can

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.680
see that it gives us the RELATION between

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.640
the object’s distance from the mirror, image’s

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.489
distance from the mirror and the focal length.

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:22.320
What if instead of this, I had placed an object

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.970
somewhere else? It wouldn’t change our formula!

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.475
The equation does not depend on the object’s

00:02:27.475 --> 00:02:29.980
position from the mirror. It is same for any

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.060
position of the object.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.879
What if instead of concave mirror, we had

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.560
convex mirror? Again, it wouldn’t change

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.060
our formula! Yes , this formula is true for

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.080
ALL types of spherical mirrors: convex as

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.450
well as concave mirrors. Now the question

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.265
is how do we derive or prove this formula?

00:02:50.265 --> 00:02:53.079
There are many ways to derive the equation

00:02:53.079 --> 00:02:54.220
but we will look at the easiest one.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.610
In order to derive this formula, we need to

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.040
know only one thing, and that is the concept

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.079
of SIMILAR TRIANGLES . You must have come

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:07.500
across similar triangles many times in our

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.140
maths class. So let’s review that first.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.800
In simple language, triangles are said to

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.550
be similar if they have the SAME SHAPE . For

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.007
instance these two triangles are similar since

00:03:19.007 --> 00:03:22.239
they have same shape. This triangle is just

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:24.505
a scaled down version of this.

00:03:24.505 --> 00:03:27.300
These two are also similar triangles.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.100
What’s so special about similar triangles?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.920
When two triangles are similar then the ratios

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.355
of their corresponding sides are equal. For

00:03:37.355 --> 00:03:40.790
instance, here ‘triangle ABC’ and ‘triangle

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.420
PQR’ are similar so, ‘AB over PQ’ is

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.900
equal to ‘BC over QR’ is equal to ‘AC

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.340
over PR’. And this fact is going to help

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.000
us derive the mirror equation!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.120
The second thing about two similar triangles

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.569
is that all the corresponding angles have

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:01.655
the same measure. For example, here

00:04:01.655 --> 00:04:05.359
‘angle A’ is equal to ‘angle P’, ‘angle B’

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.460
is equal to ‘angle Q’ and ‘angle C ’

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.680
is equal to ‘angle R’.

00:04:10.689 --> 00:04:13.748
This also works in the reverse. That is, if

00:04:13.748 --> 00:04:16.950
for any two triangles, if we prove that their

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.926
corresponding angles are equal, then they

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:23.120
are similar triangles. This is called triple

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.420
A test of similarity for proving two triangles similar.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:30.100
Similarly, if the ratios of their corresponding

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.500
sides are equal then the triangles are similar.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.960
Ok, let’s go back to our figure for the
mirror equation.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.920
Now from the top of the object, let me draw

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.960
a line that meets the tangent at point B.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.100
This line is parallel to the principal axis.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.220
And from this point on the image, let me draw

00:04:49.229 --> 00:04:52.602
a parallel line again to the tangent at point

00:04:52.602 --> 00:04:55.750
D. Note that points B and D are not on the

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.560
mirror. They’re on this tangent which is

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.660
drawn at point P.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.440
But actually both the points are very close

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.360
to each other the mirror in reality. This

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.740
is because we have seen in our previous video

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.030
that the aperture of the mirror that we are

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.360
considering is much smaller than the radius

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.590
of curvature. Because of the smaller aperture,

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.860
these distances are very small and so we can

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:20.490
assume these two points to be on the tangent.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:24.246
So we can assume these two points to be one

00:05:24.246 --> 00:05:28.090
point; and these two points to be one point.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.826
Now consider these two triangles.

00:05:30.826 --> 00:05:33.479
Are these two triangles similar?

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:35.140
Let me first just draw them separately here.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:40.020
We see that ‘angle OAF’ is equal to angle

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.260
‘DPF’. Why? They both measure ninety degrees!

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.240
What about these two angles, ‘angle OFA’

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.346
and ‘angle DFP’? When two lines intersect,

00:05:51.346 --> 00:05:54.379
the vertically opposite angles are always

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.160
equal. Hence these two angles are equal too!

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.760
What about the remaining angles? How do we

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:05.140
show that they are also equal? With very basic

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.479
logic, we know that if the two sets of corresponding

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.260
angles are equal then the third set has to

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.900
be equal . Finally we proved that triangles

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:19.082
OAF and DPF are similar by the double A or

00:06:19.082 --> 00:06:21.870
triple A test of similarity.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:23.020
Now because they’re similar, we can say

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.670
that ‘OA over DP’ is equal to ‘AF over

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:31.460
PF’ is equal to ‘OF over DF’. We are

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:34.330
not really interested in this ratio, so we

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.699
will just remove it from here.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.060
Now, from this figure, can you tell me what

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.120
AF and PF represent? [pause]

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.380
PF is the FOCAL LENGTH ‘f’ but what about

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.800
AF? We know that AP is the object’s distance

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:52.092
from the mirror which is ‘u’. But AP is

00:06:52.092 --> 00:06:55.551
equal to ‘AF plus FP’ and FP is the focal

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.560
length ‘f’! So AF is nothing but ‘u minus f'

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.180
And what are OA and DP? They are the heights

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.220
of the object and the image.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.039
Let’s denote them with ‘h o’ and ‘h i’.

00:07:09.039 --> 00:07:12.880
We are not done yet. This is not the formula

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.153
that we are looking for. Let this be equation

00:07:17.153 --> 00:07:21.521
one. Now consider triangles IGF and BPF. These

00:07:21.521 --> 00:07:23.920
two triangles are also similar again by the

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.060
triple A test. I will leave this for you to

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.180
verify.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.479
The ratios of their corresponding sides are

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:31.990
equal.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.000
I will remove this ratio, as it is not required.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.430
IG and BP are nothing but the heights of the

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.580
image and the object. PF is the focal length

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.870
‘f’. So What's GF?

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:49.180
GP is equal to GF plus FP! We know that FP

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:53.460
is ‘f’. And what is GP? Yes, it is the

00:07:53.469 --> 00:07:56.519
image’s distance from the mirror ‘v’.

00:07:56.519 --> 00:07:59.569
Therefore GF is ‘v minus f’. Let this

00:07:59.569 --> 00:08:02.120
be equation two.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.420
Now let’s invert equation 2 to get the third

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.169
equation We are almost there now. So we have these

00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:10.500
two equations now with us. They both have

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:14.690
the same term on one side of equal to sign,

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:15.190
so the other two sides will be equal.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:20.240
Cross multiplying and solving further will finally

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.090
give us the required mirror formula.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.090
 

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.090
 

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.130
Finally we have our mirror equation in front

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.360
of us! It was fun to derive it wasn’t it?

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.500
However this is not the only way to derive

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.240
the mirror equation.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.090
Now if you remember, at the start of the video

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:40.060
I told you that this is a GENERAL EQUATION.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.380
That is, this equation is valid for any position

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.140
of the object and for any spherical mirror

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.060
under consideration. But is it so? Ermm, in

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:55.400
order to use this equation, we must make sure

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.910
that some rules are followed. We will see

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.940
those rules in our next video.

